    "title": "Endpoint kernel-biform factor-degree dichotomy",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "the strict endpoint kernel biform has one irreducible parameter factor of degree at least ceil((3m+1)/4)",
    "statement": "At the strict A=3,e=m saturation-failure endpoint, factor the primitive kernel biform over F_q(X). Exactly one factor is small relative to the T-by-N incidence capacities, and its parameter degree is at least ceil((3m+1)/4). Hence the biform does not split into parameter-linear factors for m>=2, is irreducible for m=2,3,4, and has an irreducible parameter factor of degree at least 103079215105 on the official row.",
